@startuml
title The denylist as a sorted linked list - what a covering node proves

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

rectangle "**Root**\nkey = empty (-inf)\nlink -> 0x11" as ROOT
rectangle "**Node**\nkey = 0x11\nlink -> 0x77" as N11
rectangle "**Node**\nkey = 0x77\nlink -> 0x99" as N77 #FDEEEE
rectangle "**Node**\nkey = 0x99\nlink = None (+inf)" as N99

ROOT -right-> N11
N11 -right-> N77
N77 -right-> N99

note bottom of N11
  **Bob = 0x44 is NOT sanctioned.**
  This node covers him:
  0x11 < 0x44 < 0x77
  Both bounds strict, so Bob
  cannot be hiding in the gap.
end note

note bottom of N77
  **Alice = 0x77 IS sanctioned.**
  Her own node occupies the slot,
  so no gap contains her:
  node 0x11 links exactly to 0x77
  (0x77 < 0x77 fails), and her own
  node fails 0x77 < 0x77 too.
  No covering node can exist.
end note

note top of ROOT
  Each node is ONE UTxO:
  * at the denylist spend address
  * holding exactly ADA + 1 list NFT
  * key minted into the asset name
    ("Node" ++ 28-byte hash), immutable
  * link in the inline datum, mutable
end note

note top of N99
  An EMPTY denylist is just the root,
  key -inf and link +inf, which covers
  every possible party.
end note
@enduml
